Calculated Fields

Profit Margin = SUM([Profit])/SUM([Sales])
Cost = SUM([Sales])-SUM([Profit])
Average Order Value = SUM([Sales])/COUNTD([Order Id])
Return Rate = SUM([Return Flag]) / COUNTD([Order Id])
Shipping Delay Bucket = DATEDIFF('day',[Order Date],[Ship Date])

# Business Insights

1. Sales Trend
Observation
Sales remained relatively stable throughout the year with noticeable peaks in February and October.
Data Evidence
Monthly sales fluctuate between approximately 15M and 20M, with October showing the highest sales.
Business Interpretation
Demand remains consistent throughout the year, indicating stable customer purchasing behavior.
Recommended Action
Investigate marketing campaigns or seasonal factors that contributed to higher sales in February and October and replicate successful strategies.

2. Regional Performance
Observation
The South region generated the highest sales, while East and West produced similar but lower sales.
Data Evidence
South recorded approximately 64.7M in sales compared to around 49M in both East and West.
Business Interpretation
The South region has the strongest customer base and market penetration.
Recommended Action
Continue investing in South while identifying growth opportunities in East and West through targeted promotions.

3. Category Profitability
Observation
Technology is the most profitable product category by a significant margin.
Data Evidence
Technology generated over 28M profit compared with approximately 3.6M for Furniture and 1.7M for Office Supplies.
Business Interpretation
Technology products deliver substantially higher margins than other categories.
Recommended Action
Prioritize Technology products in marketing campaigns and inventory planning.


4. Customer Segment Behaviour
Observation
Home Office customers generated the highest sales among all customer segments.
Data Evidence
Home Office sales exceeded 74M, followed by Consumer (71.9M) and Corporate (70.6M).
Business Interpretation
The Home Office segment represents a valuable customer group with strong purchasing power.
Recommended Action
Develop loyalty programs and customized offers for Home Office customers.

5. Discount Impact
Observation
Higher discounts do not consistently increase profitability.
Data Evidence
The scatter plot shows several highly discounted transactions producing relatively low profits.
Business Interpretation
Aggressive discounting reduces margins without guaranteeing higher returns.
Recommended Action
Review discount policies and establish discount limits for low-margin products.

6. Shipping and Delivery Performance
Observation
Different shipping modes contribute to varying delivery performance.
Data Evidence
Delivery days vary across shipping methods, indicating operational differences.
Business Interpretation
Shipping efficiency directly affects customer satisfaction and operational cost.
Recommended Action
Evaluate slower shipping methods and improve logistics efficiency.

7. Return Pattern
Observation
Furniture has the highest return rate among all product categories.
Data Evidence
Furniture return rate is approximately 7.7%, compared with 3.7% for Office Supplies and 3.0% for Technology.
Business Interpretation
Furniture products may have quality, transportation, or customer expectation issues.
Recommended Action
Review product quality, packaging, and return reasons for Furniture products.

8. Business Risk and Opportunity
Observation
Technology delivers the highest profitability while Furniture experiences the highest return rate.
Data Evidence
Technology contributes over 28M profit, whereas Furniture has the largest proportion of returned orders.
Business Interpretation
Technology represents the strongest growth opportunity, while Furniture presents operational risk.
Recommended Action
Increase investment in Technology products while reducing Furniture return rates through quality improvement initiatives.
